[{:db/id "q-313352/field-1/5dac37105900fc9827b124e32d405933bffabb1fd0992a59fae3a29028cb3924" :answer/id #uuid "541fd7d7-6982-5f2f-9745-ea2e7808bf03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{2t+5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-313352/field-1/9ff33a29535207ffbc26d44cb372425cf27776989e54054a63daaf7c81a2e56c" :answer/id #uuid "ec95733b-0d33-5529-ad85-7dd7f7c2c51e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2t+5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-313352/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6558ba30-4c8a-5c38-8dba-a9083eb2c752" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-313352/field-1/5dac37105900fc9827b124e32d405933bffabb1fd0992a59fae3a29028cb3924" :answer-field/choices ["q-313352/field-1/5dac37105900fc9827b124e32d405933bffabb1fd0992a59fae3a29028cb3924" "q-313352/field-1/9ff33a29535207ffbc26d44cb372425cf27776989e54054a63daaf7c81a2e56c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-313352" :question/id #uuid "b678523d-2283-522f-b86f-4ebdf18393b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-313352" :question/problem "The ambient temperature in a laboratory varies over time. After $t$ seconds, the temperature (in degrees Celsius) is modeled by\n\n$$\nΘ(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t+5)+18.\n$$\n\nWhat is the instantaneous rate of change of the temperature as a function of $t?$\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change is\n{{field-1}} degrees Celsius per second." :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate of change of the temperature is ${Θ}^{′}(t).$\n\nWe take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Θ}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{d}{dt}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t+5)+18] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2t+5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change of the ambient temperature is $\\frac{2}{2t+5}$ degrees Celsius per second." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-313352/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236cec41-4836-5526-893d-e6f2a23d1801"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-313352"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343160/field-1/32f770e63fb5c35e5159111fc03a189d139dae533684d298e753883184729453" :answer/id #uuid "81a9e964-3a8a-5978-84b8-cbee3c4ae78d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10^t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343160/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "08ca6a17-131f-5149-bf73-e53b90f77f28" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-343160/field-1/32f770e63fb5c35e5159111fc03a189d139dae533684d298e753883184729453" :answer-field/choices ["q-343160/field-1/32f770e63fb5c35e5159111fc03a189d139dae533684d298e753883184729453"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343160" :question/id #uuid "8cf3f18f-5b4e-59b4-9a80-141299bdc32b" :question/math-academy-id "q-343160" :question/problem "The number of views $V,$ in millions, of a viral video after $t$ days is modeled by $V(t)=\\frac{{10}^{t}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}$ for $0\\le t\\le 6.$ What is the instantaneous rate of change of the number of views as a function of $t?$\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change is\n{{field-1}} views per day." :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate of change of the number of views is equal to ${V}^{′}(t).$ \n\nFirst, we take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{10}^{t}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{10}^{t}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡10}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10} \\\\  & ={10}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change of the number of views is ${10}^{t}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-343160/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236cec41-4836-5526-893d-e6f2a23d1801"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343160"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-86191/selection/a0ad34a6b936a005ac03b7c8ecb9b136ef3e3e7c17083a0ce94c294e009a254a" :answer/id #uuid "27d04d21-825b-59ef-bea0-e7136ff9cae3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{355}{1+{e}^{-t}}$ liters per day" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86191/selection/d27704000fd15b1c5af8e1bb9e8ed758b6d26fb00ac9c1818f9ef5390fe9cc20" :answer/id #uuid "db14086d-d818-5ca4-a619-9770d3a947e4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{710{e}^{t}}{2+{e}^{-t}}$  liters per day" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86191/selection/ab790d18bd1290e9aeae9c21441524eb45790e4b5b35b6d830b859c7aa7aae41" :answer/id #uuid "f9b91f08-9fb4-5b3f-9b4a-1814f2033caf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$355{e}^{t}$  liters per day" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86191/selection/f8e4d9ce5226aabe74e4365bdba18979d3a778dcc560af6d98db8745396cf117" :answer/id #uuid "43741ee7-1f7c-5b81-9f09-2b2714183729" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$710{e}^{-t}$  liters per day" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86191/selection/3682a49f97a1797d649ec0f68328d1e227f2aaab03fbfcd347ac2ae254cab37a" :answer/id #uuid "a52c4689-da7a-570e-8989-65b6edf76e48" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{710}{1+{e}^{-t}}$  liters per day" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86191/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5fde2b24-adb2-54a1-9c8d-6b66f11b4bbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-86191/selection/3682a49f97a1797d649ec0f68328d1e227f2aaab03fbfcd347ac2ae254cab37a" :answer-field/choices ["q-86191/selection/a0ad34a6b936a005ac03b7c8ecb9b136ef3e3e7c17083a0ce94c294e009a254a" "q-86191/selection/d27704000fd15b1c5af8e1bb9e8ed758b6d26fb00ac9c1818f9ef5390fe9cc20" "q-86191/selection/ab790d18bd1290e9aeae9c21441524eb45790e4b5b35b6d830b859c7aa7aae41" "q-86191/selection/f8e4d9ce5226aabe74e4365bdba18979d3a778dcc560af6d98db8745396cf117" "q-86191/selection/3682a49f97a1797d649ec0f68328d1e227f2aaab03fbfcd347ac2ae254cab37a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-86191" :question/id #uuid "e1a7b751-463a-5c53-9c04-73eeed9f0b75" :question/math-academy-id "q-86191" :question/problem "The function $P(t)=710\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{e}^{t})$ represents the volume of milk, in liters, produced on a farm $t$ days after the owner bought new cows. What is the instantaneous rate of change of the volume of produced milk as a function of $t?$" :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate of change of the volume of produced milk with respect to time is ${P}^{′}(t).$\n\nNow, the rate of change of $P(t)$ with respect to $t$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(710\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{e}^{t})) \\\\  & =710\\,\\frac{{e}^{t}}{1+{e}^{t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{710}{1+{e}^{-t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change of the volume of produced milk is  $\\frac{710}{1+{e}^{-t}}$ liters per day." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-86191/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236cec41-4836-5526-893d-e6f2a23d1801"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-86191"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48716/selection/b49f3399b08acf085651669fec035a05f2ce183371c04c4fe9d2f7491c655e60" :answer/id #uuid "fdd3244c-a0a0-5c88-bcb4-5872c40df7f5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$s(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡s+1)$ squared millimeters per centimeter" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48716/selection/8fb1ff018203b3b73e770c1140d1f203509ddf06af4b474c45ab11f076724399" :answer/id #uuid "9339905b-5c41-59ae-b1b2-46a86b0d3058" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2\\operatorname{ln}⁡s+1$ squared millimeters per centimeter" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48716/selection/a85ee11383cc8247ea2e70d528eb66c768747f74607604e4a0e2585cb4ed1529" :answer/id #uuid "b8a34102-0865-5c83-a41a-d820e8889a0b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡s$ squared millimeters per centimeter" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48716/selection/e4f5a573cc38eccfb1c1f99a49b706bfd24ec8e7a248169af7b48a876d3484e9" :answer/id #uuid "3ac030bf-d209-5cc9-83da-88109f66b52e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${s}^{2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡s-1)$ squared millimeters per centimeter" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48716/selection/260686bb71d81947ffb079dd4b0e37ca474425a57f26bb1610f2516cda1b6924" :answer/id #uuid "426c8adb-a5b5-5c02-988a-1a63e3d80136" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$s(\\operatorname{ln}⁡s+2)$ squared millimeters per centimeter" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48716/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3e7c9d67-6032-5733-b728-8bfef8996e77" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48716/selection/b49f3399b08acf085651669fec035a05f2ce183371c04c4fe9d2f7491c655e60" :answer-field/choices ["q-48716/selection/b49f3399b08acf085651669fec035a05f2ce183371c04c4fe9d2f7491c655e60" "q-48716/selection/8fb1ff018203b3b73e770c1140d1f203509ddf06af4b474c45ab11f076724399" "q-48716/selection/a85ee11383cc8247ea2e70d528eb66c768747f74607604e4a0e2585cb4ed1529" "q-48716/selection/e4f5a573cc38eccfb1c1f99a49b706bfd24ec8e7a248169af7b48a876d3484e9" "q-48716/selection/260686bb71d81947ffb079dd4b0e37ca474425a57f26bb1610f2516cda1b6924"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48716" :question/id #uuid "32646f68-3349-52fa-be3e-4f5c20ecb8ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-48716" :question/problem "The function $L(s)={s}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡s$ models the surface area of a flower's petal, in squared millimeters, as the flower's stem grows to a length of $s$ centimeters, where $s>1.$ What is the instantaneous rate of change of the surface area as a function of $s?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}({s}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡s) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}({s}^{2})\\operatorname{ln}⁡s+{s}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡s) \\\\  & =(2s)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡s+{s}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{s}) \\\\  & =2s\\operatorname{ln}⁡s+s \\\\  & =s(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡s+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate change of the surface area is $s(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡s+1)$ squared millimeters per centimeter." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-48716/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236cec41-4836-5526-893d-e6f2a23d1801"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48716"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343161/field-1/db165208654506fc062511bed6341fe6de6d2db91a622101b16f47c87fc23a11" :answer/id #uuid "17011bf5-8813-572c-b8db-fd204a43fbae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12e^{-2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343161/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "047c645f-3050-55fa-bba8-3898778ad76e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-343161/field-1/db165208654506fc062511bed6341fe6de6d2db91a622101b16f47c87fc23a11" :answer-field/choices ["q-343161/field-1/db165208654506fc062511bed6341fe6de6d2db91a622101b16f47c87fc23a11"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343161" :question/id #uuid "04f190f8-b0ca-50fd-afc4-814a3c316fe0" :question/math-academy-id "q-343161" :question/problem "The function $C(t)=6{e}^{-2t}$ gives the concentration, in milligrams per liter, of a medication in the bloodstream $t$ hours after administration. Find the instantaneous rate of change of the concentration as a function of $t.$\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change of the concentration is\n{{field-1}}\nmilligrams per liter per hour." :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate of change of the concentration is equal to ${C}^{′}(t).$\n\nNow, the rate of change of $C(t)$ with respect to $t$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{e}^{-2t}) \\\\  & =6(-2){e}^{-2t} \\\\  & =-12{e}^{-2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change of the concentration is $-12{e}^{-2t}$ milligrams per liter per hour." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-343161/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236cec41-4836-5526-893d-e6f2a23d1801"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343161"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-2439/selection/43f28230735d11c7a908fdc97c5247cb15fe991e3923dc7bcbb729aa84f2e731" :answer/id #uuid "dd113f46-4b31-5b41-bad2-d251fbd9afae" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4$ pounds per year" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2439/selection/3445f95f797412666ea807e2ca8527e5d3dceacb3134848dfb58a7f7ff1f190d" :answer/id #uuid "47f8fa86-94c2-57b4-a020-597ffe2519df" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$15$ pounds per year" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2439/selection/a4c6b8d0338baf17e713cc8d818d2354752555e20bbb82472ce47e723fbe4724" :answer/id #uuid "265e5f09-9052-5578-afb6-fc447db085b9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$7$ pounds per year" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2439/selection/08ded1e832f7a76c7e48b4f7fb26cb2067f8d965584f1d2d3a1725803a2558ce" :answer/id #uuid "8870a406-8412-5751-b14a-5f7961b137c3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$5$ pounds per year" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2439/selection/1b555bb5422391180f9326877128ad3efd9d4492ad3545d8601cae43f46187d6" :answer/id #uuid "8fb54627-a2fe-53a7-8424-00b9cc09f24a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$10$ pounds per year" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2439/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "569cc057-bc84-5009-b10e-ba39b9d6c179" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-2439/selection/1b555bb5422391180f9326877128ad3efd9d4492ad3545d8601cae43f46187d6" :answer-field/choices ["q-2439/selection/43f28230735d11c7a908fdc97c5247cb15fe991e3923dc7bcbb729aa84f2e731" "q-2439/selection/3445f95f797412666ea807e2ca8527e5d3dceacb3134848dfb58a7f7ff1f190d" "q-2439/selection/a4c6b8d0338baf17e713cc8d818d2354752555e20bbb82472ce47e723fbe4724" "q-2439/selection/08ded1e832f7a76c7e48b4f7fb26cb2067f8d965584f1d2d3a1725803a2558ce" "q-2439/selection/1b555bb5422391180f9326877128ad3efd9d4492ad3545d8601cae43f46187d6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-2439" :question/id #uuid "105b150c-115a-581d-a5ed-c12e12c6e2a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-2439" :question/problem "The weight $w,$ in pounds, of a baby gorilla $t$ years after birth can be modeled by the function $w(t)=4{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}+15.$ What is the instantaneous rate of change of his weight when $t=1$ year?" :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate of change of weight when $t=1$ year is equal to ${w}^{′}(1).$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}+15) \\\\  & =12{t}^{2}-2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}^{′}(1) & =12(1)^{2}-2(1) \\\\  & =12-2 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate change of the weight when $t=1$ year is $10$ pounds per year." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-2439/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff5ec0b-1456-5231-94e1-0fc5923d6672"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-2439"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-72352/selection/2384bbee3bcbc18fc8b19ba8c225cbd5fde07856cbb4675d31ffe46d1bd4e958" :answer/id #uuid "ff3ea3a0-0252-57e3-aeec-232b99135da4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3$ meters per second" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72352/selection/8f94bb4b240324b0991e3db4874f14f0b26102c94ea631327925a9767a8dd91c" :answer/id #uuid "b8fb16e8-cf8a-5273-9f9e-97b4fbe73eba" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$5$ meters per second" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72352/selection/76721bbb1426e202f47db91fe21aa3cefb05e17951e056cfd0f3fc96664896d6" :answer/id #uuid "1e3f02ef-59c7-5837-a6c2-9d92c02c90d2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4$ meters per second" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72352/selection/c6fd78c8ed16508645fd0ef7fc54ff18cb5afd4fec1f4c2b88ea6e25dc27128a" :answer/id #uuid "0445507a-2423-5178-bf12-706b5c412c22" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$ meters per second" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72352/selection/2d4c0919269a3acb4d95f4de03fc376648bed8e7e60c4f82ab3afe0667c66f20" :answer/id #uuid "96f05212-4e3a-599e-92ef-43d04918b0f3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$ meter per second" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72352/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8e1d0e37-098a-5943-85a3-515d49a429e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72352/selection/2384bbee3bcbc18fc8b19ba8c225cbd5fde07856cbb4675d31ffe46d1bd4e958" :answer-field/choices ["q-72352/selection/2384bbee3bcbc18fc8b19ba8c225cbd5fde07856cbb4675d31ffe46d1bd4e958" "q-72352/selection/8f94bb4b240324b0991e3db4874f14f0b26102c94ea631327925a9767a8dd91c" "q-72352/selection/76721bbb1426e202f47db91fe21aa3cefb05e17951e056cfd0f3fc96664896d6" "q-72352/selection/c6fd78c8ed16508645fd0ef7fc54ff18cb5afd4fec1f4c2b88ea6e25dc27128a" "q-72352/selection/2d4c0919269a3acb4d95f4de03fc376648bed8e7e60c4f82ab3afe0667c66f20"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72352" :question/id #uuid "2e527e4e-1ea7-5d39-a401-6a8d7982a17f" :question/math-academy-id "q-72352" :question/problem "The function $x(t)={t}^{2}+t$ models the distance traveled by a car $t$ seconds after it sets off on a journey. Find the instantaneous rate at which the distance traveled by the car is changing with respect to time when $t=1$ second." :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate at which the distance traveled by the car is changing when $t=1$ second is equal to ${x}^{′}(1).$\n\nTaking the derivative, the rate of change of $x(t)$ with respect to $t$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+t)=2t+1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand evaluating at $t=1$ gives\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(1)=2(1)+1=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate at which the distance traveled by the car is changing when $t=1$ second is $3$ meters per second." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-72352/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff5ec0b-1456-5231-94e1-0fc5923d6672"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72352"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48742/selection/e2ae2c49a0c5c7863df09b79944532a477078b54180d31913b28d29578a020d6" :answer/id #uuid "5d2e8223-aa73-5fdf-b1c8-a06201a1ea66" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{3}$ dollars per gallon" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48742/selection/2c294d6a0f96e32fff462e60c384f81b15db52483262964ae69998a0e74b20fa" :answer/id #uuid "970f8a8e-ae8d-5083-9796-939275e798f2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{3}{4}$ dollars per gallon" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48742/selection/eb97a2a46e1dae007718e14df1800330c2bddf56e828db98b41ea200eeed53cc" :answer/id #uuid "d81dde64-6e4e-5f3c-81b1-edc328a772aa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{4}{3}$ gallons per dollar" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48742/selection/da9678db73025d8b5be4526d39cbf6247e12571b4cec5c2985d138b0e33720d5" :answer/id #uuid "637f4574-bbd3-5b60-a12e-f4585452c817" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-\\frac{3}{4}$ gallons per dollar" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48742/selection/23f2d14ca35c30972b29627ff516edd4611239942c70a02323c9b68fcdea9858" :answer/id #uuid "c5a9fcf4-cb9b-5f03-b7fe-30629a356cb3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-\\frac{4}{3}$ dollars per gallon" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48742/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4bed608d-f02e-5aeb-a964-2ac240b404ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48742/selection/23f2d14ca35c30972b29627ff516edd4611239942c70a02323c9b68fcdea9858" :answer-field/choices ["q-48742/selection/e2ae2c49a0c5c7863df09b79944532a477078b54180d31913b28d29578a020d6" "q-48742/selection/2c294d6a0f96e32fff462e60c384f81b15db52483262964ae69998a0e74b20fa" "q-48742/selection/eb97a2a46e1dae007718e14df1800330c2bddf56e828db98b41ea200eeed53cc" "q-48742/selection/da9678db73025d8b5be4526d39cbf6247e12571b4cec5c2985d138b0e33720d5" "q-48742/selection/23f2d14ca35c30972b29627ff516edd4611239942c70a02323c9b68fcdea9858"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48742" :question/id #uuid "9aa60056-cf3e-58e8-bae0-fd58cc5adfa3" :question/math-academy-id "q-48742" :question/problem "The function $P(v)=\\frac{2v+50}{v+1}$ models the price at which gas is sold, in dollars, depending on the volume $v$ sold the previous day, in gallons. What is the instantaneous rate of change of the price of gas when $v=5$ gallons?" :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate of change of the price when $v=5$ gallons is equal to ${P}^{′}(5).$\n\nNow, we take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{′}(v) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}v}(\\frac{2v+50}{v+1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}v}(2v+50)\\cdot (v+1)-(2v+50)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}v}(v+1)}{(v+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2)\\cdot (v+1)-(2v+50)\\cdot (1)}{(v+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2v+2-2v-50}{(v+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{48}{(v+1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $v=5$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{′}(5) & =-\\frac{48}{((5)+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{48}{36} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate change of the price when $v=5$ gallons is $-\\frac{4}{3}$ dollars per gallon." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-48742/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff5ec0b-1456-5231-94e1-0fc5923d6672"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48742"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-72358/selection/dcd25d27668ee3923ccb6fc778d139bb57989bbca5f78636b4df89c9f4ef9b69" :answer/id #uuid "a98ba616-2146-5601-8995-23f7f9943b16" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{11}{16}$ cubic centimeters per second" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72358/selection/d4d2dde2ec2a5447ce32dafda8d7875dc730cce5f37cd9c0ab25afaf184066de" :answer/id #uuid "2c148a25-b71b-5184-a328-e2b08a144dca" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{7\\sqrt{30}}{60}$ cubic centimeters per second" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72358/selection/28a8784f88bd09392d96e5468c203f5da7645a90d813ddbe1745ab9d138ee227" :answer/id #uuid "6191f350-adf2-5192-8d13-f3556935fdd5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{7}{16}$ cubic centimeters per second" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72358/selection/203cb0c25f564329fcbc8b3200e36a01045e09be7b4ba215cdefa3cbb55835c1" :answer/id #uuid "cb3273a8-5ad5-5ef4-b480-ff5dca96b779" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{7}{8}$ cubic centimeters per second" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72358/selection/06abd8466fc35fb901c0a4f4dca9abc2389f771d999afbe9748aa6155d112891" :answer/id #uuid "e5a47853-b09d-5433-ac5d-3e6ed2b7945e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{11}{8}$ cubic centimeters per second" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72358/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "13329ba6-19a3-5419-817c-1900d14a9f79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72358/selection/203cb0c25f564329fcbc8b3200e36a01045e09be7b4ba215cdefa3cbb55835c1" :answer-field/choices ["q-72358/selection/dcd25d27668ee3923ccb6fc778d139bb57989bbca5f78636b4df89c9f4ef9b69" "q-72358/selection/d4d2dde2ec2a5447ce32dafda8d7875dc730cce5f37cd9c0ab25afaf184066de" "q-72358/selection/28a8784f88bd09392d96e5468c203f5da7645a90d813ddbe1745ab9d138ee227" "q-72358/selection/203cb0c25f564329fcbc8b3200e36a01045e09be7b4ba215cdefa3cbb55835c1" "q-72358/selection/06abd8466fc35fb901c0a4f4dca9abc2389f771d999afbe9748aa6155d112891"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72358" :question/id #uuid "072688e5-9941-5223-b2ce-40292e03ba47" :question/math-academy-id "q-72358" :question/problem "The volume $V$ (in cubic centimeters) of water in a pail $s$ seconds after it starts filling can be modeled by the function $V(s)=7\\sqrt{s}+2.$ Find the instantaneous rate at which the volume of water is changing with respect to time at the moment when the volume of water in the pail is equal to $30$ cubic centimeters." :question/worked-solution "Since we are given that the volume of water in the pail is $30$ cubic centimeters, the time can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}30 & =7\\sqrt{s}+2 \\\\ 7\\sqrt{s} & =28 \\\\ \\sqrt{s} & =4 \\\\ s & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe instantaneous rate at which the volume of water in the pail is changing when $s=16$ seconds is equal to ${V}^{′}(16).$\n\nTaking the derivative, the rate of change of $V(s)$ with respect to $s$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(7\\sqrt{s}+2) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(7{s}^{1/2}+2) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}{s}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{s}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand evaluating at $s=16$ gives\n\n$$\n{V}^{′}(16)=\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{16}}=\\frac{7}{8}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate at which the volume of water in the pail is changing when $s=16$ seconds is $\\frac{7}{8}$ cubic centimeters per second." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-72358/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff5ec0b-1456-5231-94e1-0fc5923d6672"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72358"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-2440/selection/1d34e626092588f9083f01ff65b5a1f85407fb60934f066f71283e9c4873bdb5" :answer/id #uuid "19dcd5e9-a528-5f53-8401-723f3102e1b1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3$ feet per second" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2440/selection/e555b4a28e306d41ba0648e486c949fec385b07d2f34480ee580c424d976a930" :answer/id #uuid "7e250424-4f2a-5df5-aa00-435d6f055dab" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$18$ feet per second" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2440/selection/15692ff2a2e3f1cfab6c78cc1fb65368c8c8bdcd919479e30295d38042c15f67" :answer/id #uuid "cacd8cb5-9238-502f-9314-081400ee8678" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$14$ feet per second" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2440/selection/6aee3ed3e1c2aa1f27bfad029cc60d721451ab48dff88485690b15445aa03944" :answer/id #uuid "09baa327-ca7e-5fd5-bfa5-68d13e65d39a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$16$ feet per second" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2440/selection/e48313e3ea65ec73dd0f6350cb74a3c448ba125d674aa848c45df2ff988499e7" :answer/id #uuid "a80084d7-549c-5701-821f-8596e309d18b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$27$ feet per second" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2440/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f5058cad-a6d2-5186-93b0-037fea9994dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-2440/selection/6aee3ed3e1c2aa1f27bfad029cc60d721451ab48dff88485690b15445aa03944" :answer-field/choices ["q-2440/selection/1d34e626092588f9083f01ff65b5a1f85407fb60934f066f71283e9c4873bdb5" "q-2440/selection/e555b4a28e306d41ba0648e486c949fec385b07d2f34480ee580c424d976a930" "q-2440/selection/15692ff2a2e3f1cfab6c78cc1fb65368c8c8bdcd919479e30295d38042c15f67" "q-2440/selection/6aee3ed3e1c2aa1f27bfad029cc60d721451ab48dff88485690b15445aa03944" "q-2440/selection/e48313e3ea65ec73dd0f6350cb74a3c448ba125d674aa848c45df2ff988499e7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-2440" :question/id #uuid "9f34cdca-0767-505c-ad6b-beadde1398f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-2440" :question/problem "A particle moves in a straight line so that after $t$ seconds it is $p(t)={t}^{3}-11t+9$ feet from its initial position. What is the instantaneous rate of change of the particle's position when $t=3$ seconds?" :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate of change of the particle's position when $t=3$ seconds is equal to ${p}^{′}(3).$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-11t+9) \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, substituting $t=3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{′}(3) & =3(3)^{2}-11 \\\\  & =27-11 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate change of the particle's position when $t=3$ seconds is $16$ feet per second." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-2440/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff5ec0b-1456-5231-94e1-0fc5923d6672"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-2440"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343488/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "dc267a72-1f12-5e44-ac07-7ea51933d449" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343488/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "eb503e3b-bd00-53f1-9498-3d66c0c6d75d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343488/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6700395d-dcc7-5086-a186-e754b313d392" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-343488/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-343488/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-343488/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343488" :question/id #uuid "e6e2654a-5b06-5727-b889-b8068e0655c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-343488" :question/problem "The bases of a trapezoid are increasing and the larger base is always three times the smaller base. The height of the trapezoid is $3\\,cm.$ Find the rate of change of the area of the trapezoid with respect to its smaller base $b.$\n\nThe rate of change of the area of the trapezoid with respect to its smaller base is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The area of a trapezoid is given by \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{(B+b)h}{2},\n$$\n\n where $b$ is the smaller base, $B$ is the larger base and $h$ is the height of the trapezoid.\n\nWe are given that $B=3b$ and $h=3,$ so we can express the area $A$ as a function of the base $b$ by substituting $B=3b$ and $h=3$ in the formula above. We get\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{(b+3b)(3)}{2}=6b.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $A(b)$ with respect to $b$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(b) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}b}(6b) \\\\  & =6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}b}(b) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-343488/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20b289d4-96a7-5d1b-9714-6afabab4804d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343488"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-48725"] :question/worked-solution "The area of a rectangle is given by  \n\n$$\nA=bh,\n$$\n\n where $b$ is the base and $h$ is the height of the rectangle.\n\nWe are given that $h=10b,$ so we can express the area $A$ as a function of the base $b$ by substituting $h=10b$ in the formula above. We get\n\n$$\nA=b(10b)=10{b}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $A(b)$  with respect to $b$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(b) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}b}(10{b}^{2}) \\\\  & =10\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}b}({b}^{2}) \\\\  & =10(2b) \\\\  & =20b.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-48720/selection/480b7929d39d2e41128fc857c105b6b53ac9d32767d2bf5e1a8865046879d086" :answer/id #uuid "e0487cbf-9e86-5200-b92d-2893b59f2778" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}/\\text{cm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48720/selection/c893a33b06f406aa16cff160dded3bcbed161c42207d13c008a23f8040d0b87d" :answer/id #uuid "29941a62-a075-51e5-97c6-0e2aa7f969a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}/\\text{cm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48720/selection/db8fe6b090f1d697614c4d23373538490fa2da7d139468e780735a13c2f767f1" :answer/id #uuid "fdedc5d1-9be8-57bd-920d-21e25bb00022" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48720/selection/fc2b596bb813342e18222b67cb300b304c2e02fff54649bddfb8dac5916175cc" :answer/id #uuid "ddff0772-8081-50bd-bdf9-7468b4f7f3cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}/\\text{cm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48720/selection/2ed0d5282c51805290c6d233ce60b4c4f514f7abbd9f2efe2cdc8c1801ded47d" :answer/id #uuid "793e2126-ee2e-507f-8e8f-3047f3ee0415" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48720/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3b70f361-4268-5e3f-81d5-197dd437dd57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48720/selection/c893a33b06f406aa16cff160dded3bcbed161c42207d13c008a23f8040d0b87d" :answer-field/choices ["q-48720/selection/480b7929d39d2e41128fc857c105b6b53ac9d32767d2bf5e1a8865046879d086" "q-48720/selection/c893a33b06f406aa16cff160dded3bcbed161c42207d13c008a23f8040d0b87d" "q-48720/selection/db8fe6b090f1d697614c4d23373538490fa2da7d139468e780735a13c2f767f1" "q-48720/selection/fc2b596bb813342e18222b67cb300b304c2e02fff54649bddfb8dac5916175cc" "q-48720/selection/2ed0d5282c51805290c6d233ce60b4c4f514f7abbd9f2efe2cdc8c1801ded47d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48720" :question/id #uuid "9ae90c2c-65ba-5cd2-9c97-71c571033581" :question/math-academy-id "q-48720" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948186/assets/2b5d589462bf2477be3d305ea88f3d5462b7d6ea4e001a9a71790d53e1683665.png)\n\nThe area of a square is increasing. Find the instantaneous rate at which the area of a square is increasing with respect to the length of its side at the moment when the length of the sides is equal to $l=6\\,\\text{cm}.$" :question/worked-solution "We know that the area of the square with respect to $l$ is given by  \n\n$$\nA=A(l)={l}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTaking the derivative, the rate of change of $A(l)$  with respect to $l$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(l) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}l}({l}^{2})=2l,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand evaluating at $l=6$ gives\n\n$$\n{A}^{′}(6)=2(6)=12.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate at which the area of the square is increasing when the length of the side is $l=6\\,\\text{cm}$ is $12\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}/\\text{cm}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-48720/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20b289d4-96a7-5d1b-9714-6afabab4804d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48720"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343491/field-1/3c6830c9764386f438a560b99e49bfa21f63aa27d1236f22a30ebe133905a846" :answer/id #uuid "a5ef0793-fcfe-5a86-a983-7d6d08b5b9af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{C}{2\\pi}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343491/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e4389edc-42c9-5ff5-9a82-4f1fd486b205" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-343491/field-1/3c6830c9764386f438a560b99e49bfa21f63aa27d1236f22a30ebe133905a846" :answer-field/choices ["q-343491/field-1/3c6830c9764386f438a560b99e49bfa21f63aa27d1236f22a30ebe133905a846"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343491" :question/id #uuid "7d1e4fcd-7cd2-516b-a124-a0f04de90c73" :question/math-academy-id "q-343491" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948186/assets/c63dfe563c07b143bdc7cc28ab4d1142bea8c455be31ce924fa310c5e4903305.png)\n\nThe area $A$ of the circular disk above is changing as the circle expands. The circumference and radius of the circle are $C$ and $r,$ respectively. \nFind the rate of change of the area of the circle with respect to its circumference.\n\nThe rate of change of the area of the circle with respect to its circumference $C$ is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The area of a circle is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\pi {r}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the circle.\n\nWe know that $C=2\\pi r,$ so we can express the area $A$ as a function of the circumference $C$ by substituting $r=\\frac{C}{2\\pi }$ into the formula above. We get\n\n$$\nA=\\pi {r}^{2}=\\pi {(\\frac{C}{2\\pi })}^{2}=\\frac{{C}^{2}}{4\\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $A(C)$ with respect to $C$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(C) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}C}(\\frac{{C}^{2}}{4\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\pi }\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}C}({C}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\pi }(2C) \\\\  & =\\frac{C}{2\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-343491/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20b289d4-96a7-5d1b-9714-6afabab4804d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343491"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48715/selection/4510989d27ad573337f7a88b8d9e57799134f9d47b97d40874881e500ea7cbe3" :answer/id #uuid "b75dfa85-a23c-5b8f-9414-d11d295bcd2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {r}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48715/selection/90db78b903778798668f0296c2ffe72f5e5d9baec8d0a3424b0caea00e96ef8a" :answer/id #uuid "15f613d9-aaf6-5a5c-9d18-db16165e9752" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\pi {r}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48715/selection/d01cc5d1b4b4923e09105ef3b731a67b9c9eabb3abcd4c0c6f1437c422e42544" :answer/id #uuid "17e16d7f-97a1-5726-9c8c-ecaba05f1d54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4{r}^{2}}{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48715/selection/7f00338e8679ad3675d52ae609d16fd80c0850243076b1daa7f899746095397f" :answer/id #uuid "a6abc8f3-6154-5ec0-8d43-d76ae7573582" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\pi {r}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48715/selection/1a2c3881891ab7eca8aa4af8d7002d84b8252f633df18da1be453e64ebd8a8b4" :answer/id #uuid "e5785436-cf1f-5158-8c54-edccd93d2c30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48715/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "145f7fee-116c-5748-a964-4c69b5e8340d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48715/selection/90db78b903778798668f0296c2ffe72f5e5d9baec8d0a3424b0caea00e96ef8a" :answer-field/choices ["q-48715/selection/4510989d27ad573337f7a88b8d9e57799134f9d47b97d40874881e500ea7cbe3" "q-48715/selection/90db78b903778798668f0296c2ffe72f5e5d9baec8d0a3424b0caea00e96ef8a" "q-48715/selection/d01cc5d1b4b4923e09105ef3b731a67b9c9eabb3abcd4c0c6f1437c422e42544" "q-48715/selection/7f00338e8679ad3675d52ae609d16fd80c0850243076b1daa7f899746095397f" "q-48715/selection/1a2c3881891ab7eca8aa4af8d7002d84b8252f633df18da1be453e64ebd8a8b4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48715" :question/id #uuid "b9da3be8-6213-5e5a-b4d1-baa350c7d90b" :question/math-academy-id "q-48715" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948186/assets/4915dc00f10fa5edc911cf9744e99e662b705898b32f16391805c7733b8f89e5.png)\n\nThe volume $V$ of the sphere above is increasing. The radius of the sphere is $r.$ Find the rate of change of the volume of a sphere with respect to its radius." :question/worked-solution "The volume of the sphere is given by \n\n$$\nV=V(r)=\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $V(r)$ with respect to $r$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}^{′}(r) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}r}(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}r}(\\pi {r}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot 3\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =4\\pi {r}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-48715/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20b289d4-96a7-5d1b-9714-6afabab4804d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48715"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
